  "title": "Red Hat Security Advisory: php:8.2 security update",
  "description": "A critical security update for PHP 8.2 addresses multiple vulnerabilities including out-of-bounds read/write, use-after-free, request smuggling, cross-site scripting (XSS), signature bypass, information disclosure, remote code execution, and denial of service. These vulnerabilities affect PHP components such as PHP-CGI, PHP-FPM, PHAR, SOAP, and session handling. The update is available for Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.8 Extended Update Support and related variants.",
